<body>
    <h1>Cola Increase Table</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;border-colo=
r: #998DD9;border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;">
<p>FORTRA Review Complete 10.10.2025</p>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Proposed Solution</strong></p>
<p><strong>Functional Summary</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Each renewal quote line will include a COLA Uplift % field.</p></li>
<li>
<p>This field is automatically populated during renewal quote creation by q=
uerying a Custom Metadata Type (CMDT) that stores uplift percentages by Sol=
ution Name.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Solution Name will be pulled directly from the Product linked to each qu=
ote line.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If no matching entry is found in CMDT, the uplift will default to 0%.</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>Users can manually override the uplift % on individual quote lines after=
 creation. Once edited, the automation will not overwrite the value.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>The pricing application mechan<a class=3D"external-link" data-card-appea=
rance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://helpsystems.atlassian.net/browse/SC-933" r=
el=3D"nofollow">https://helpsystems.atlassian.net/browse/SC-933</a>ism (e.g=
., Price Rule, Action, Flow, Apex) is flexible and can be selected by the R=
CA development team based on best fit.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Logic and Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Quote Line Creation</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<p>When each renewal quote line is created:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Retrieve the Solution Name from the associated Product.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Query COLA_Uplift_Rules (CMDT) for a record with a matching Solution Nam=
e.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If a match is found, set:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>COLA_Uplift_Percent__c =3D Default_Uplift_Percent__c from CMDT</p></li>
<li>
<p>Default_COLA_Uplift_Percent__c =3D same CMDT value (read-only reference)=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>If no match is found, set both fields to 0%.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Both values are stored directly on the quote line record for pricing and=
 reference.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p><strong>Uplift Calculation</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<p>=C2=B7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apply the uplift =
during pricing using the formula:</p>
<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final Price =3D Base Renewal Price =C3=97 (1 + COLA_=
Uplift_Percent__c / 100)</p>
<p>=C2=B7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; COLA_Uplift_Perce=
nt__c is always sourced from the quote line field, not directly from CMDT. =
This ensures that any user override is respected during price calculation.<=
/p>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p><strong>User Override Behavior</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Users may edit the COLA_Uplift_Percent__c field on the quote line after =
creation.</p></li>
<li>
<p>When this field is updated, the system will automatically reprice the li=
ne using the new value.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The automation will not recalculate or overwrite the field after the ini=
tial creation, even if the quote is recalculated or CMDT values are changed=
 later.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Users can not update the Default_COLA_Uplift_Percent__c field.</p>
